# {{ .SchemaName }} Implementation Scaffolds

This directory contains implementation scaffolds for the `{{ .SchemaName }}` API.

These scaffolds implement the interfaces defined in the generated API module at:
`{{ .ModulePath }}`

## Directory Structure

```
{{- range .Namespaces }}
{{ . }}/
├── implementation.go    # Implementation struct with dependencies
{{- $namespace := . }}
{{- range $.Endpoints }}
{{- if eq .Namespace $namespace }}
├── {{ toSnakeCase .ShortImplName }}.go    # {{ .ShortImplName }}() method
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
```

## Usage

### 1. Import the generated API module

```go
import (
    api "{{ .ModulePath }}"
{{- if .IsPublic }}
    orm "{{ .ORMModule }}"
{{- end }}
    types "{{ .TypesModule }}"

    // Import your implementations (scaffolds live in internal/route-impl/<namespace>)
{{- range .Namespaces }}
    "your-project/internal/route-impl/{{ . }}"
{{- end }}
)
```

### 2. Create implementation instances

```go
{{- range .Namespaces }}
{{- if $.IsPublic }}
{{ . }}Impl := {{ . }}.NewImplementation(db, logger)
{{- else }}
{{ . }}Impl := {{ . }}.NewImplementation(logger)
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
```

### 3. Register routes with the chi router

```go
r := chi.NewRouter()

err := api.RegisterRoutes(r, api.Config{
{{- if .IsPublic }}
    DB:             db,
{{- end }}
    Logger:         logger,
    Implementations: api.Implementations{
{{- range .Namespaces }}
        {{ toGoName . }}: {{ . }}Impl,
{{- end }}
    },
})
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}
```

## Implementing Endpoints

Each endpoint method is stubbed with a `not implemented` error. To implement an endpoint:

1. Open the corresponding file (e.g., `auth/login.go`)
2. Replace the stub implementation with your business logic
3. Use the dependencies from the Implementation struct

## Namespace Interfaces

Each namespace implements an interface defined in the generated API module:

{{- range .Namespaces }}

### {{ toGoName . }}Implementation

```go
type {{ toGoName . }}Implementation interface {
{{- $namespace := . }}
{{- range $.Endpoints }}
{{- if eq .Namespace $namespace }}
    {{ .ShortImplName }}(ctx context.Context{{- range .PathParams }}, {{ .Name }} {{ .GoType }}{{- end }}{{- range .QueryParams }}, {{ .Name }} {{ if .IsArray }}[]{{ else if not .Required }}*{{ end }}{{ .GoType }}{{- end }}{{- if .Filterable }}, filters []filterparse.Filter{{- end }}{{- if .HasInput }}, input *types.{{ .InputType }}{{- else if .ScalarArgs }}{{- range .ScalarArgs }}, {{ .Name }} {{ .GoListType }}{{- end }}{{- end }}{{- if .HasFileUpload }}, files map[string]*api.FileUploadData{{- end }}) ({{- if .OutputIsArray }}{{ .OutputGoListType }}{{- else }}*{{ .OutputGoType }}{{- end }}, error)
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
}
```
{{- end }}

## Notes

- Scaffolds are written to the path in `scaffoldsOutputDir` (e.g. `services/web-api/internal/route-impl`)
- These scaffold files are generated once and never overwritten
- Feel free to modify, refactor, and reorganize as needed
- Add tests alongside your implementations (e.g., `auth/login_test.go`)
- The generated API module handles HTTP parsing, validation, and routing
- Your implementations focus purely on business logic
